      "type": "concept",
      "definition": "The Middle Horizon (roughly 600–1000 CE) is archaeology's label for the period when the Wari and Tiwanaku empires spread a common art style and iconography across most of the central Andes — the era between the earlier patchwork of regional cultures and the later post-imperial fragmentation."
