    {
      "term": "Chen Chen",
      "matchText": "Chen Chen",
      "wikiSlug": "",
      "type": "place",
      "definition": "Chen Chen was one of the largest Tiwanaku colonies in the Moquegua Valley of southern Peru — a full-scale settlement on the valley floor with Tiwanaku-style ceramics, architecture, and burials, occupied through the Middle Horizon a few miles downhill from the rival Wari fortress at Cerro Baúl."
    },
    {
      "term": "Cerro Echenique",
      "matchText": "Cerro Echenique",
      "wikiSlug": "",
      "type": "place",
      "definition": "Cerro Echenique was a Tiwanaku colonial settlement in the Moquegua Valley, one of the cluster of valley-floor sites (with Omo and Chen Chen) that marked Tiwanaku's reach into the same southern valley where the Wari had built their frontier outpost at Cerro Baúl."
    }
  ],
