      "matchText": "Anita Cook",
      "wikiSlug": "",
      "type": "people",
      "definition": "An Andean archaeologist whose work on Wari iconography and statecraft helped reframe Wari as a planned imperial state with a coherent administrative ideology."
    },
    {
      "term": "Patrick Williams",
      "matchText": "Patrick Williams",
      "wikiSlug": "",
      "type": "people",
      "definition": "An archaeologist who, with Donna Nash, directed the long-running excavations at the Wari colony of Cerro Baúl in the Moquegua valley — the central case study for how Wari and Tiwanaku coexisted on the same frontier."
    },
    {
      "term": "Donna Nash",
      "matchText": "Donna Nash",
